==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From Pre-Finnic ''*konïš'', borrowed from Pre-Germanic ''*gn̥ni̯o-'', compare Old Norse {{m|non|kyn||wonder}}. The original meaning in Finnish was ''magic'', from  which  
only recently ''machine''. <ref>[http://www.sgr.fi/sust/sust266/sust266_kallio.pdf The Prehistoric Germanic Loanword Strata in Finnic]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{fi-IPA|*}}
* {{rhymes|e|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|ko|ne|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[machine]]
# [[appliance]] {{gloss|apparatus or device, typically powered electrically, used in homes to perform domestic functions}}
#: ''[[kodinkone|kodin'''kone''']], [[kotitalouskone|kotitalous'''kone''']]'' -- [[household appliance|household '''appliance''']]
# ''short for'' {{m|fi|lentokone||airplane}}

